# QA / staging environment — template. Copy to `.ai/qa/test-env.env`, which is
# gitignored, and fill in. Never commit the filled-in copy.
#
# The four required application variables.
DATABASE_URL='postgresql+psycopg://trip_planner:trip_planner@127.0.0.1:55432/trip_planner_qa'
SESSION_SECRET=''   # python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))'
APP_BASE_URL='http://localhost:8000'
ENVIRONMENT='development'

# --- The reservation inbox (optional) --------------------------------------
#
# Leave every INBOX_* line unset to run with the inbox off — that is a supported
# state and the one QA exercises unless it is testing the inbox itself. Setting
# some but not all of the four required ones is refused at startup.
#
# See the README's "The reservation inbox" section for the AWS side: the receipt
# rule with scanning enabled, the MX record, the private encrypted bucket with
# its 30-day lifecycle, the HTTPS SNS subscription with raw delivery OFF, and
# the SQS dead-letter queue.

# INBOX_RECIPIENT='inbox@mail.planner.example.com'
# INBOX_AWS_REGION='eu-central-1'
# INBOX_SNS_TOPIC_ARN='arn:aws:sns:eu-central-1:123456789012:trip-planner-inbound'
# INBOX_S3_BUCKET='trip-planner-inbound-mime'

# Optional, with their defaults.
# INBOX_S3_PREFIX=''
# INBOX_ALLOWED_SENDERS=''
# INBOX_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES='41943040'

# No AWS credential belongs in this file. The app reads S3 through the standard
# credential chain, so give the QA environment a least-privilege role (or the
# usual AWS_* variables in the shell that launches it) scoped to GetObject and
# DeleteObject on the bucket's INBOX_S3_PREFIX.

# --- Routing: the model that reads a confirmation (optional, and separate) ---
#
# Leave unset to run the inbox without routing — mail still arrives, is stored
# and is placeable by hand. One provider is selected explicitly; there is no
# fallback, and only the selected provider's key is read.
#
# Before enabling: review that provider's data-retention and training terms.
# What leaves is a confirmation — a name, an itinerary, booking references.

# INBOX_MODEL_PROVIDER='anthropic'      # anthropic | gemini | openai
# INBOX_MODEL_NAME=''                   # the provider's small/cheap tier
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''                  # or GEMINI_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY
# GEMINI_API_KEY=''
# OPENAI_API_KEY=''

# The EU-residency / gateway knob. Must be https://.
# INBOX_MODEL_BASE_URL=''

# The budget FAILS CLOSED: with any of these three unset, no call is made.
# INBOX_MODEL_MONTHLY_BUDGET=''
# INBOX_MODEL_INPUT_PRICE=''
# INBOX_MODEL_OUTPUT_PRICE=''
